==Strategy==
==='''Chapter 1'''===
Be careful of Zir Zeals area attack freeze for 3 seconds and his 1500 range burrow, which gets him past every unit you'll have in the main fight already.

When combined with Imperator Sael and his area slow, the 2 seal partners can catch sleepy players off guard. Together they can shred through front lines and get to the base/newly spawned units if you're not proactive.

As always, bring any Zombie Killer or "Massive damage to Zombies" unit to help keep the Zombies at bay! Anti-Alien units will still be a big help and are highly recommended, more so than Anti-Angel units(Ramen is still helpful of course).
*This stage can be rushed due to the lack of a boss shockwave but this will only work in chapter 1 as the units in chapter 2 have high health.

==='''Chapter 2'''===
This stage may present a bit of a struggle with no peons to farm early and a couple pretty well buffed Mistress Celeboodle to deal with. Even with all Alien treasures unlocked, they took quite some time to kill and with their double damage buff they can make quick work of your front line, especially with little cash at the start. For this reason, cheap meatshields are recommended over ones like Maximum the Fighter or Cameraman Cat.

You'll have anywhere from 2-3 Mistresses stacked up at the start of the stage as you save up for your Ubers or Anti-Alien units to spawn in.

As you're fighting all these poodles, you'll start to see a couple Hyppoh and Zomboe work their way up to you in addition to another Heavenly Hippoe or two. These will finally provide you with some decent money.

Once you're starting to clear out the assortment of hippoes you will see a group of 3 Imperator Sael and Zir Zeal heading down your way. This is the time you need to have Zombie Freezers or Zombie Killer units on reserve due to Zir Zeals very long burrow range.
*As many Treasures as possible are recommended here due to the Mistress' large health pool and the pressure that a group of Imperator Sael can put on your squad with Slowing Area attacks. Any Zombie treasures from CotC will obviously help too but the zombies aren't truly the main threat here.

*You have very little time to farm Cat Worker levels so if this stage is giving you trouble a Rich Cat can be used to help out early. Sniper cat can also buy you a little time with the early Celeboodles.

==='''Chapter 3'''===
The major differences here are the massively buffed enemies and the stacking of said enemies. Be ready for 3 Imperator Saels all in a single stack, which can prove devastating if you don't have a Weaken or Freeze effect for them. The Mistress Celeboodles still don't have much in the way of HP but they can shred your meatshields if you're not careful.

There will be a point where your meatshields are separated and you're fighting a Zir Zeal in your back lines but don't panic and keep the units spawning.

The good news is that you only have the single Zir Zeal to worry about and once he's down you have a clear path to the finish.

